  "problem": "The relationship between the number of cars $n$ Steve washes in $t$ hours is shown in the following table:\n\n| Hours  ($t$) | Cars ($n$) |\n| --- | --- |\n| $1$ | $4$ |\n| $3$ | $12$ |\n| $5$ | $20$ |\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. There is **not** a proportional relationship between $n$ and $t.$\n\nII. The constant of proportionality is $4.$\n\nIII. There is a proportional relationship between $n$ and $t.$",
